  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support of Limited-mobiity Vulnerable Evacuees in Kharkiv region (SOLVE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtRCC proposes a multi-sectoral intervention in Kharkiv region aimed to:lt/pgtltulgtltligtupgrade and expand reception capacity in collective sites, providing&#xa0;safe, dignified, inclusive and&#xa0;accessible accommodationlt/ligtltligtprovide specialized services, assistance and referralslt/ligtlt/ulgtltpgtfor the newly-evacuated and internally-displaced people, with strong focus&#xa0;on people with&#xa0;mobility limitations,&#xa0;including persons with disabilities, older persons, and individuals with chronic illnesses.ltbrgtThis is planned to be achieved through:ltbrgtlt/pgtltulgtltligtcollective sites identification and selectionlt/ligtltligtrenovation and adaptation (care  maintenance/site improvement)ltbrgtlt/ligtltligtprovision of essential equipmentlt/ligtltligtsupport of safe and participatory site management and governance structuresltbrgtlt/ligtltligtindividual protection assistance (cash)lt/ligtltligtcase management and referral serviceslt/ligtlt/ulgtltpgtRCC posesses prior&#xa0;experience&#xa0;and existing capacities for the implementation of&#xa0;all of the proposed activities under the project, subject to funding availability.ltbrgtlt/pgtltpgtRCC intends to implement the project in close coordination with the relevant stakeholders, including CCCM and Protection clusters,&#xa0;UHF, OCHA, relevant authorities, departments and services, relevant partners and&#xa0;beneficiaries.ltbrgtProject activities implementation, management and monitoring will be maintained through a robust organizational structure, including dedicated management, program and support&#xa0;teams.lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
